<p>A paper kite, that soared on high,<br />
While looking down was able to descry<br />
A joyous butterfly,<br />
And cried, &#8220;We faintly see your foolish efforts zealous;<br />
Confess that you are rather jealous,<br />
When you behold our elevated lot.&#8221;<br />
&#8220;Jealous? Oh, surely not.<br />
Your grandeur is a phantom, or an empty vision,<br />
Your tethered flight awakes, believe me, but derision;<br />
Can happiness be got from an existence ever fettered?<br />
And how could life for me be bettered?<br />
As I aspire I venture higher,<br />
And never, solely for another&#8217;s idle leisure<br />
And pleasure,<br />
Lose freedom I desire.&#8221;</p>
<p>&#8212; Ivan Krylov</p>
